
(Vox OS Core Utilities)
A text called "Program Version" is "0.1.10".

(Parse the flags now)
A flag called "out file" is "--out" or "-o", it is a text with default "write-output".
A flag called "wants help" is "--help" or "-h", it is a boolean.
A flag called "wants version" is "--version" or "-v", it is a boolean.
A text called "Program" is arguments's name.

To "show version".
  Print "{Program} (voxos) {Program Version} by Josjuar Lister".
  Exit 0.

If "wants help" then,
  Print "{Program} - Read from stdin and write to a file",
  Print "Usage: {Program} [OPTION]... --out FILE",
  Print "\nOptions:",
  Print "  -h, --help   display this help and exit",
  Print "  -v, --version output version information and exit",
  Print "  -o, --out    the file to write to (default: write-output)",
  Print "\nExamples:",
  Print "\t{Program} --out output.txt < input.txt \tWrite the contents of input.txt to output.txt",
  Print "See https://github.com/vox-lang/vox for more information.",
  Exit 0.

Create a buffer called "file contents".
Create a buffer called "input line".

Open a file for reading at "/dev/stdin" called stdin.
Open a file for writing at 'out file' called "file handle".

while true,
  Read line from stdin into 'input line',
  If 'input line' is "/save\n" then,
    write 'file contents' to 'file handle',
    exit 0.
  Append 'input line' to 'file contents'.
